From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rowley <johnrowleyster@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:29:49 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Implement IDirectDraw4 and IDirectDrawSurface4 in miniwin

EnumDisplayModes lists the classic resolutions and the display's own in
the display format (MINIWIN_PIXELFORMAT, else the desktop's), honouring
DDENUMRET_CANCEL and a filter description. CreateSurface, Lock,
GetSurfaceDesc, Blt, Flip and GetAttachedSurface take DDSURFACEDESC2 and
DDSCAPS2 and share the version-1 code. SetDisplayMode and
GetAvailableVidMem are implemented.

Blits follow DirectDraw more closely: a 16-bit fill colour is a pixel in
the surface's format, the source colour key applies only with
DDBLT_KEYSRC/DDBLTFAST_SRCCOLORKEY, Lock honours its rectangle,
GetSurfaceDesc reports the pitch, SetColorKey no longer fails on SDL3's
boolean success, and a surface can read back the framebuffer.

With MINIWIN_PIXELFORMAT the framebuffer's transfer buffer uses the
display format. GetDeviceCaps reports BITSPIXEL and PLANES, and
IDirectDrawClipper::SetClipList succeeds. MINIWIN_DUMP_FRAME=<file>
writes each presented frame to a file for headless runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

